WEBVTT

00:03:16.840 --> 00:03:20.170
<b>Quest 01          The RPG That Begins with "Nice to Meet You"</b>

00:03:32.270 --> 00:03:35.010
All right! We beat the dragon!

00:03:35.350 --> 00:03:36.770
We did it!

00:03:45.030 --> 00:03:47.030
<b>Seiga Academy</b>

00:03:58.880 --> 00:04:00.990
Hey, let's go check it out sometime!

00:04:00.990 --> 00:04:01.550
Great idea!

00:04:31.590 --> 00:04:34.040
Please present your ID card.

00:04:35.040 --> 00:04:36.120
Okay.

00:04:38.950 --> 00:04:40.580
Give me a second.

00:04:40.890 --> 00:04:43.170
Are you really one of our students?

00:04:43.170 --> 00:04:45.190
Yeah, I'm in class 2-B.

00:04:45.190 --> 00:04:46.700
You're awfully suspicious.

00:04:46.700 --> 00:04:48.180
I promise I'm not.

00:04:48.620 --> 00:04:51.080
No, you definitely are.

00:04:51.080 --> 00:04:52.470
He definitely is.

00:04:53.400 --> 00:04:55.530
He's a Seiga Academy student.

00:04:56.670 --> 00:04:59.940
He's Tachibana Itsuki-kun from class 2-B.

00:04:59.940 --> 00:05:00.870
What?

00:05:00.870 --> 00:05:02.790
Izumi-san, you know him?

00:05:03.090 --> 00:05:03.940
No.

00:05:04.270 --> 00:05:08.200
The student council president knows 
the faces and names of every student.

00:05:08.200 --> 00:05:11.010
Ah, I wouldn't expect any less from her.

00:05:11.010 --> 00:05:13.580
You, look for it again.

00:05:13.580 --> 00:05:14.710
O-Okay.

00:05:18.040 --> 00:05:20.180
Rules are rules.

00:05:20.450 --> 00:05:21.960
And things have been dangerous lately.

00:05:22.770 --> 00:05:23.960
Thanks for your hard work.

00:05:24.930 --> 00:05:26.210
There it is!

00:05:26.720 --> 00:05:28.000
I found it.

00:05:28.000 --> 00:05:29.900
See? I'm not suspicious after all.

00:05:29.900 --> 00:05:32.350
Save that for after your card checks out.

00:05:32.350 --> 00:05:33.220
Okay, okay.

00:05:33.980 --> 00:05:36.730
Um, thanks.

00:05:43.720 --> 00:05:44.970
Oh, right.

00:05:47.130 --> 00:05:49.450
See? I'm not suspicious.

00:05:50.930 --> 00:05:52.490
Hey, Itsuki.

00:05:52.950 --> 00:05:54.220
You're back, huh?

00:05:54.220 --> 00:05:55.240
Took you long enough.

00:05:55.240 --> 00:05:56.750
Hey, Kota.

00:05:57.070 --> 00:06:00.810
I roused the guard's suspicion 
because I couldn't find my card.

00:06:00.810 --> 00:06:02.500
That's unfortunate.

00:06:02.940 --> 00:06:04.980
Izumi-senpai, welcome back.

00:06:04.980 --> 00:06:05.910
Thank you.

00:06:05.910 --> 00:06:08.470
It's good to see you again. This is for you.

00:06:08.470 --> 00:06:10.760
I'll cherish this.

00:06:11.030 --> 00:06:16.270
We prayed super hard for you 
to pass the national exam.

00:06:16.750 --> 00:06:19.020
Thank you. I'll do my best.

00:06:19.400 --> 00:06:21.450
You must've really enjoyed 
your summer vacation

00:06:21.450 --> 00:06:23.930
if you're coming back on the very last day.

00:06:23.930 --> 00:06:26.040
There's nothing to do at the dorm.

00:06:26.040 --> 00:06:28.780
And it's not like anyone's waiting for me.

00:06:29.190 --> 00:06:30.080
Oh, right.

00:06:30.080 --> 00:06:32.600
My sister told me to share 
these with my friends.

00:06:37.880 --> 00:06:40.040
How was Chizuru-neesan?

00:06:40.370 --> 00:06:42.420
She was moaning and groaning 
about finding a job.

00:06:42.790 --> 00:06:45.300
She was furrowing her brow like this.

00:06:45.300 --> 00:06:47.510
What a waste.

00:06:47.510 --> 00:06:50.290
She'll ruin her good looks if she does that.

00:06:50.290 --> 00:06:52.010
Hey, Tachibana.

00:06:52.010 --> 00:06:53.710
Long time, no see.

00:06:53.710 --> 00:06:56.060
That looks good. I'm taking this.

00:06:57.240 --> 00:06:59.310
Kota, you wanna play tonight?

00:06:59.310 --> 00:07:02.990
Sorry, but I'm not doing 
anything until after the meet.

00:07:02.990 --> 00:07:03.910
Oh, right.

00:07:04.190 --> 00:07:05.710
Another time, then.

00:07:06.040 --> 00:07:07.720
What was that about?

00:07:07.720 --> 00:07:09.070
<i>PSO2</i>.

00:07:09.370 --> 00:07:11.070
<i>PSO2</i>?

00:07:11.550 --> 00:07:13.080
I told you about it before.

00:07:13.080 --> 00:07:17.050
It's <i>Phantasy Star Online 2</i>,
 or <i>PSO2</i> for short.

00:07:17.050 --> 00:07:19.170
I told you to give it a try.

00:07:20.300 --> 00:07:22.330
I seem to recall you mentioning 
something like that.

00:07:22.620 --> 00:07:27.160
You know, if you're not playing 
online games in this day and age,

00:07:27.160 --> 00:07:28.840
you'll get left behind.

00:07:28.840 --> 00:07:32.080
Yeah, right. It's just a game, right?

00:07:38.430 --> 00:07:39.600
Seiga Academy Student Council
1 New Mail

00:07:46.600 --> 00:07:50.430
<i>Message for Tachibana 
Itsuki-sama of class 2-B.</i>

00:07:50.720 --> 00:07:53.270
<i>Tomorrow, after finishing 
your club activities,</i>

00:07:53.270 --> 00:07:56.200
<i>report to the student council room 
in the main building at six o'clock.</i>

00:07:56.540 --> 00:07:58.280
<i>I have an important message for you.</i>

00:07:58.580 --> 00:08:00.790
<i>Sincerely, Student Council 
President Izumi Rina.</i>

00:08:01.670 --> 00:08:03.460
The student council president?

00:08:04.720 --> 00:08:06.990
<i>The opening ceremony will begin shortly.</i>

00:08:06.990 --> 00:08:10.080
<i>Students, please report to the auditorium.</i>

00:08:09.420 --> 00:08:10.080
Wha—?!

00:08:10.080 --> 00:08:11.800
What?!

00:08:12.110 --> 00:08:15.940
You received an invitation from Izumi-senpai?

00:08:15.940 --> 00:08:17.510
Yeah, for after school.

00:08:17.510 --> 00:08:20.250
When did you and Izumi-senpai 
become good enough friends

00:08:20.250 --> 00:08:22.060
to start emailing each other?

00:08:22.410 --> 00:08:25.990
Actually, we just started.

00:08:27.560 --> 00:08:29.400
Don't give me that.

00:08:29.400 --> 00:08:31.160
Why are you acting so smug?

00:08:31.160 --> 00:08:32.730
I'm joking.

00:08:32.730 --> 00:08:34.520
It wasn't a personal invitation.

00:08:34.520 --> 00:08:36.570
It was an official message 
from the student council.

00:08:36.940 --> 00:08:38.810
Ah, there he is!

00:08:38.810 --> 00:08:39.870
Tachibana!

00:08:40.240 --> 00:08:41.770
Hey. What's up?

00:08:42.050 --> 00:08:44.370
Sorry, but could you give us a hand again?

00:08:44.370 --> 00:08:47.380
It's just a practice game, 
but a first-year caught a cold.

00:08:47.990 --> 00:08:50.340
Sure, as long as we're done before six.

00:08:50.340 --> 00:08:52.450
Thanks for the help.

00:08:59.670 --> 00:09:01.850
She's always so beautiful.

00:09:07.350 --> 00:09:12.360
It seems like Izumi-senpai is 
always surrounded by people.

00:09:13.980 --> 00:09:18.850
As the headmaster mentioned earlier,

00:09:17.860 --> 00:09:21.860
<b>Opening Ceremony</b>

00:09:18.850 --> 00:09:21.860
the second semester is an important 
time for us third years.

00:09:22.290 --> 00:09:25.140
Additionally, we'll be 
holding the school festival,

00:09:25.140 --> 00:09:26.870
a major event for the academy.

00:09:27.720 --> 00:09:32.070
I'd like to take this year's festival as
an opportunity to strengthen the bonds

00:09:32.070 --> 00:09:34.880
between all members of the academy.

00:09:35.450 --> 00:09:36.140
Huh?

00:09:35.450 --> 00:09:39.480
Let's make this a festival 
that couldn't have been done

00:09:36.140 --> 00:09:39.270
Come to think of it, isn't Vice President
 Mishima-san missing?

00:09:39.480 --> 00:09:42.370
without every student's participation.

00:09:39.580 --> 00:09:44.110
She's studying abroad, so she withdrew 
from school over the summer.

00:09:42.370 --> 00:09:44.890
I hope I'll have your support.

00:09:44.110 --> 00:09:44.890
Seriously?

00:09:48.580 --> 00:09:53.030
I heard Izumi-senpai ranked in the nation's
top percentile in August's mock exams.

00:09:53.510 --> 00:09:55.680
She's an outstanding athlete, too.

00:09:55.680 --> 00:09:58.780
She does great at everything
 <i>and</i> looks good doing it.

00:09:58.780 --> 00:10:01.050
But despite that, she's not haughty about it.

00:10:01.780 --> 00:10:05.300
It's no wonder she's Seiga Academy's 
once-in-a-decade stand-out student,

00:10:05.300 --> 00:10:07.290
the star of Seiga!

00:10:10.690 --> 00:10:12.540
Thank you!

00:10:14.550 --> 00:10:16.300
Thanks for waiting.

00:10:17.810 --> 00:10:19.300
Thank you.

00:10:19.740 --> 00:10:21.420
Thanks, Tachibana.

00:10:21.420 --> 00:10:24.160
You made some good passes, 
and the captain was happy about it.

00:10:24.440 --> 00:10:27.680
It's no wonder they call you the master sub.

00:10:27.950 --> 00:10:31.440
I know you actually call me "the handyman."

00:10:31.440 --> 00:10:33.460
It's a compliment.

00:10:33.460 --> 00:10:37.070
Anyway, you handle everything 
thrown at you pretty well.

00:10:38.450 --> 00:10:42.820
<i>Another way of saying 
"pretty well" is "just okay."</i>

00:10:43.500 --> 00:10:47.340
<i>In other words, I never do
 better than "just okay."</i>

00:10:43.600 --> 00:10:44.460
Did you hear?

00:10:44.460 --> 00:10:48.010
In Chiba, an unmanned train ran out of 
control in the middle of the night.

00:10:47.740 --> 00:10:51.460
<i>Maybe the rest of my life 
will be "just okay," too.</i>

00:10:48.010 --> 00:10:49.710
I saw that online.

00:10:49.710 --> 00:10:52.930
Near my parents' house, there was a car 
accident in the middle of the night.

00:10:51.900 --> 00:10:53.610
<i>No dramatic changes.</i>

00:10:52.930 --> 00:10:56.470
But not only was no one injured, 
there wasn't a single person at the scene.

00:10:53.610 --> 00:10:55.460
<i>An ordinary, "just okay" life.</i>

00:10:55.870 --> 00:10:59.910
Yesterday, I fell asleep with 
autorun on while questing.

00:10:59.910 --> 00:11:01.220
Me, too.

00:11:01.220 --> 00:11:04.040
Hey, it's already six. Let's eat.

00:11:04.320 --> 00:11:05.720
Six?

00:11:08.300 --> 00:11:10.980
The president told you to be here at six.

00:11:15.650 --> 00:11:17.030
Sorry.

00:11:17.480 --> 00:11:20.760
How could you be so thoughtless as to keep 
the student council president waiting?

00:11:20.760 --> 00:11:22.050
You think this is a joke?

00:11:22.050 --> 00:11:24.580
President, I'm against this.

00:11:24.580 --> 00:11:25.850
I agree.

00:11:26.130 --> 00:11:26.950
Me, too.

00:11:27.500 --> 00:11:29.500
The matter has already been decided.

00:11:29.500 --> 00:11:31.230
It's not up for debate.

00:11:31.540 --> 00:11:32.460
Isn't that right?

00:11:33.200 --> 00:11:34.550
Tachibana Itsuki-kun.

00:11:34.850 --> 00:11:35.710
Yes?

00:11:36.470 --> 00:11:40.470
I'm appointing you the student council
 vice president as of today.

00:11:41.460 --> 00:11:42.470
What?

00:11:42.740 --> 00:11:47.220
And as vice president, 
this is your first task.

00:11:49.390 --> 00:11:51.730
<i>PSO2</i>?

00:11:51.730 --> 00:11:56.310
<b>[PSO2] </b>(Pee Ess Oh Two)
An abbreviation of "Phantasy Star Online 2," an online RPG that gained popularity with youth worldwide as widespread use of Ethernet helped realize high speed communication.

00:11:56.310 --> 00:12:00.890
<b>[ARKS]
</b>The organization to which the player characters of "PSO2" belong. Based around the interplanetary fleet "ORACLE," it operates on various planets to wipe out the "Darkers," who seek to invade and destroy all of space.

00:12:02.180 --> 00:12:04.910
What? Teach you how to play <i>PSO2</i>?

00:12:05.780 --> 00:12:06.980
I see.

00:12:06.980 --> 00:12:11.940
So you finally feel like trying "the RPG 
that begins with 'nice to meet you.'"

00:12:11.940 --> 00:12:15.080
It's the student council 
vice president's job.

00:12:15.080 --> 00:12:16.820
Student council vice president?

00:12:17.120 --> 00:12:17.860
Who?

00:12:18.150 --> 00:12:19.060
Me.

00:12:19.060 --> 00:12:19.920
What?!

00:12:20.260 --> 00:12:22.420
That's a very appropriate reaction.

00:12:22.420 --> 00:12:24.900
You're the vice president? Why?

00:12:25.180 --> 00:12:29.180
Because my grades are pretty decent 
and my attendance is perfect.

00:12:29.660 --> 00:12:31.930
Is our student council okay?

00:12:32.260 --> 00:12:33.940
I'm wondering the same thing.

00:12:45.680 --> 00:12:47.080
I'm sorry,

00:12:47.080 --> 00:12:50.200
but we need to find a replacement 
for Mishima-san immediately.

00:12:50.200 --> 00:12:52.820
Then you should hold an election.

00:12:53.140 --> 00:12:56.440
I'm solely responsible for 
managing the student council.

00:12:56.440 --> 00:12:58.710
We haven't consented to this decision.

00:12:59.190 --> 00:13:00.810
But during second semester,

00:13:00.810 --> 00:13:04.200
between formulating next year's budget, 
helping students prepare for exams,

00:13:04.490 --> 00:13:07.710
and the academy's biggest event,
 the school festival,

00:13:07.710 --> 00:13:10.390
the student council needs help
 from everyone and their cat.

00:13:10.800 --> 00:13:12.890
In other words, you're just a cat.

00:13:12.890 --> 00:13:15.900
At least treat me like a human!

00:13:15.900 --> 00:13:18.910
You've got a lot of nerve for a mere cat.

00:13:19.250 --> 00:13:20.900
Why me?

00:13:21.200 --> 00:13:26.780
Your grades and lifestyle make you a 
suitable candidate for the student council,

00:13:26.780 --> 00:13:29.160
and you're not a member of any club.

00:13:29.640 --> 00:13:31.910
In other words, I've got 
nothing better to do.

00:13:32.500 --> 00:13:34.410
Will you help us?

00:13:35.040 --> 00:13:36.160
Sure.

00:13:36.160 --> 00:13:38.170
Don't get the wrong idea.

00:13:38.170 --> 00:13:40.490
The president isn't asking you to help.

00:13:40.490 --> 00:13:41.560
She's ordering you to help.

00:13:41.560 --> 00:13:42.700
I am asking him!

00:13:42.700 --> 00:13:46.680
You mustn't refuse the president's request.

00:13:46.680 --> 00:13:47.930
You understand that, don't you?

00:13:48.300 --> 00:13:51.990
Yeah, but why play something like <i>PSO2</i>?

00:13:51.990 --> 00:13:54.160
Something like <i>PSO2</i>?

00:13:55.530 --> 00:14:02.320
The academy requires me to create
 and submit reports on <i>PSO2</i>.

00:14:02.780 --> 00:14:05.070
Submit reports to the academy? Why?

00:14:05.520 --> 00:14:09.470
To obtain an accurate understanding 
of the academy's social network

00:14:09.470 --> 00:14:10.440
and report on it.

00:14:10.440 --> 00:14:13.540
The student council's 
purpose is to demonstrate

00:14:13.540 --> 00:14:16.330
a style of management 
appropriate for this academy.

00:14:16.620 --> 00:14:17.700
Got it?

00:14:18.260 --> 00:14:20.160
I don't get it.

00:14:20.160 --> 00:14:20.860
He's an idiot.

00:14:20.860 --> 00:14:21.590
An idiot.

00:14:23.000 --> 00:14:25.350
I'd like you to play <i>PSO2</i>

00:14:25.350 --> 00:14:29.290
and report your thoughts 
on your experience to me.

00:14:29.630 --> 00:14:32.350
But I don't really play games.

00:14:32.720 --> 00:14:35.600
Aren't you pretty good at everything?

00:14:35.920 --> 00:14:39.850
They do call you the handyman of clubs.

00:14:41.310 --> 00:14:43.140
At the very least, I can play games.

00:14:43.140 --> 00:14:46.110
Though I'll probably be just okay at it.

00:14:46.640 --> 00:14:49.180
I expect great things from you. Thanks.

00:14:53.870 --> 00:14:57.120
<b>Lessons with Kota!
PSO2, the game that begins with "Nice to meet you!"
Beginner's Guide
First! Why is this handwritten?!
Because that's my policy!
Anyway, it's already installed on your PC, so just click on it and you'll be OK!!</b>

00:14:54.600 --> 00:14:57.120
I'm taking a break from <i>PSO2</i> right now.

00:14:57.620 --> 00:15:01.120
I can't log in with you, 
but I'll show you what to do.

00:15:02.290 --> 00:15:04.360
First, I'll start the game.

00:15:06.180 --> 00:15:10.950
<i>PSO2</i> is an online RPG set is space.

00:15:11.260 --> 00:15:15.320
As a member of the planetary 
investigation organization ARKS,

00:15:15.320 --> 00:15:19.360
the player goes to various 
planets to do missions.

00:15:21.020 --> 00:15:23.360
Next up, creating my character.

00:15:24.200 --> 00:15:26.360
This looks like it'll take some time.

00:15:27.480 --> 00:15:28.990
<b>Randomize All</b>

00:15:27.480 --> 00:15:29.740
<b>Accessory Selection</b>

00:15:27.480 --> 00:15:29.740
<b>Edit Voice</b>

00:15:27.480 --> 00:15:29.740
<b>Save Data</b>

00:15:27.480 --> 00:15:29.740
<b>Randomize All</b>

00:15:28.240 --> 00:15:29.740
I'll just randomize it.

00:15:28.990 --> 00:15:29.740
<b>Randomize All</b>

00:15:32.530 --> 00:15:34.840
Hey, that looks like me!

00:15:34.840 --> 00:15:35.790
This'll do.

00:15:35.780 --> 00:15:37.960
Now to choose a name.

00:15:35.790 --> 00:15:36.030
<b>Accept</b>

00:15:35.790 --> 00:15:38.790
Enter Name

00:15:35.790 --> 00:15:38.790
<b>Cancel</b>

00:15:36.030 --> 00:15:36.280
<b></b>I

00:15:36.030 --> 00:15:38.790
<b>Accept</b>

00:15:36.280 --> 00:15:36.530
<b></b>Itsu

00:15:36.530 --> 00:15:38.790
<b></b>Itsuki

00:15:41.650 --> 00:15:44.090
President, shouldn't we get going?

00:15:44.360 --> 00:15:45.820
I want to finish this first.

00:15:45.820 --> 00:15:47.080
You go on ahead.

00:15:47.080 --> 00:15:48.050
B-But...

00:15:49.120 --> 00:15:50.300
Good work today.

00:15:50.920 --> 00:15:53.900
See you later, then.

00:15:56.140 --> 00:15:57.400
U-Um...

00:15:57.400 --> 00:15:58.060
What?

00:15:58.420 --> 00:16:01.560
What's your favorite food?

00:16:03.780 --> 00:16:05.060
Monkfish liver.

00:16:05.420 --> 00:16:06.300
What?

00:16:06.960 --> 00:16:08.340
I see...

00:16:10.440 --> 00:16:11.930
Monkfish liver, huh?

00:16:12.650 --> 00:16:14.070
I'll look up how to make it.

00:16:18.570 --> 00:16:20.910
For my weapon, I'll use...

00:16:20.910 --> 00:16:26.420
<b>BANG BANG BANG
SLASH SLASH SLASH
The Gunslash! You can shoot and cut with it! Super versatile!!</b>

00:16:21.370 --> 00:16:22.830
The gunslash.

00:16:22.830 --> 00:16:25.230
You can melee or shoot with it, huh?

00:16:25.230 --> 00:16:26.420
Sounds good.

00:16:26.760 --> 00:16:29.670
Okay, let's give it a shot!

00:16:44.020 --> 00:16:45.800
Your team disbanded?

00:16:45.800 --> 00:16:47.690
We weren't compatible.

00:16:47.970 --> 00:16:50.190
Are these all in-game characters?

00:16:51.280 --> 00:16:52.600
Nice to meet you.

00:16:54.760 --> 00:16:55.890
SORO?

00:16:56.520 --> 00:16:59.420
Did you just start today?

00:17:00.200 --> 00:17:01.260
Yeah.

00:17:01.520 --> 00:17:02.680
A robot?

00:17:02.680 --> 00:17:04.320
A CAST, then.

00:17:04.320 --> 00:17:07.480
If you'd like, I can offer you some advice.

00:17:07.480 --> 00:17:08.200
What?

00:17:08.200 --> 00:17:10.610
I'm actually a veteran player.

00:17:10.610 --> 00:17:12.960
It's been a while since 
I started playing <i>PSO2</i>.

00:17:14.260 --> 00:17:15.440
I see.

00:17:15.740 --> 00:17:17.340
He's not an NPC,

00:17:17.340 --> 00:17:21.720
but a character being controlled 
by an online player like me.

00:17:22.570 --> 00:17:24.680
I'm just trying to be nice.

00:17:24.680 --> 00:17:27.670
Anyway, no need to act tough. 
Relax your shoulders.

00:17:27.670 --> 00:17:29.420
I'm not acting tough.

00:17:29.420 --> 00:17:32.180
You don't need to thank me.

00:17:32.480 --> 00:17:33.640
Don't worry.

00:17:33.960 --> 00:17:34.610
U-Uh...

00:17:34.610 --> 00:17:37.860
It's only natural for a 
veteran to help a beginner.

00:17:38.100 --> 00:17:38.700
Well, actually...

00:17:38.700 --> 00:17:41.740
Now, let's be off on an endless adventure!

00:17:43.730 --> 00:17:44.650
Whoa there.

00:17:48.410 --> 00:17:50.680
You truly are lucky.

00:17:50.680 --> 00:17:53.460
I actually just changed classes, too.

00:17:53.460 --> 00:17:54.910
Changed classes? Like at school?

00:17:54.910 --> 00:17:57.560
So I can level with you.

00:17:57.840 --> 00:18:00.440
It must be chance that 
brought us together today.

00:18:00.440 --> 00:18:01.720
No, destiny!

00:18:02.070 --> 00:18:04.220
You really don't have to do this.

00:18:04.560 --> 00:18:06.100
<i>There's been an emergency.</i>

00:18:06.100 --> 00:18:09.230
<i>The ARKS ship city is 
under attack by Darkers.</i>

00:18:09.770 --> 00:18:14.080
<i>All ARKS members, use the Quest 
Counter to help immediately.</i>

00:18:15.480 --> 00:18:16.880
I'm going to this.

00:18:16.880 --> 00:18:18.120
Hey, wait.

00:18:18.120 --> 00:18:20.740
Emergency quests are too hard for beginners.

00:18:21.440 --> 00:18:22.730
Thanks for the invite.

00:18:22.730 --> 00:18:24.740
This is my first emergency.

00:18:36.110 --> 00:18:37.910
This is the city?

00:18:41.100 --> 00:18:43.950
Where am I supposed to go for the emergency?

00:18:47.100 --> 00:18:48.480
Wh-What is that?

00:18:49.000 --> 00:18:50.020
A bug?

00:18:50.020 --> 00:18:52.230
No, wait. Is this a Darker?

00:19:00.120 --> 00:19:01.270
Eggs?

00:19:36.650 --> 00:19:37.610
Are you okay?

00:19:37.610 --> 00:19:40.860
Th-Thanks for saving me.

00:19:51.080 --> 00:19:52.170
Now's your chance.

00:19:52.170 --> 00:19:53.030
Got it.

00:19:57.170 --> 00:19:58.550
Damn it.

00:20:00.080 --> 00:20:01.460
What am I supposed to do?

00:20:01.460 --> 00:20:03.400
Switch to gun mode!

00:20:03.690 --> 00:20:04.680
Gun?

00:20:05.420 --> 00:20:06.690
Oh, right!

00:20:12.400 --> 00:20:14.290
Its weak spot is facing our way.

00:20:14.290 --> 00:20:15.150
Aim for that!

00:20:15.590 --> 00:20:16.900
Got it!

00:20:19.590 --> 00:20:20.530
Dodge that!

00:20:21.430 --> 00:20:22.740
Easier said than done.

00:20:34.140 --> 00:20:36.760
Aim for the head, right?

00:20:42.250 --> 00:20:43.800
Did I kill it?

00:20:44.230 --> 00:20:45.440
Nice job.

00:20:45.440 --> 00:20:49.060
I can't believe you made that headshot 
without using the aim assist.

00:20:50.240 --> 00:20:52.310
Head... What?

00:20:52.620 --> 00:20:54.130
Don't be afraid to fail.

00:20:54.470 --> 00:20:57.240
You should be proud of who you are.

00:20:57.240 --> 00:21:02.820
The courage to take on adventures 
will make your soul shine.

00:21:04.580 --> 00:21:06.320
Itsuki-kun.

00:21:06.760 --> 00:21:08.410
See you tomorrow.

00:21:11.000 --> 00:21:12.830
He's better than I expected.

00:21:13.360 --> 00:21:14.920
Will he be back tomorrow?

00:21:22.340 --> 00:21:23.840
<b>PSO2</b> Report
<b>Tachibana Itsuki</b>

00:21:26.320 --> 00:21:27.420
How did it go?

00:21:27.420 --> 00:21:28.610
Just okay.

00:21:29.860 --> 00:21:33.600
This is the vice president's job, right?

00:21:33.920 --> 00:21:34.740
Yes.

00:21:34.740 --> 00:21:35.780
I'll do it.

00:21:35.780 --> 00:21:37.330
After all, I'm the vice president.

00:21:37.330 --> 00:21:38.350
Thanks.

00:21:38.780 --> 00:21:41.900
However, no matter how into <i>PSO2</i> you get,

00:21:42.380 --> 00:21:44.900
don't let your current grades slip.

00:21:45.300 --> 00:21:46.220
What?

00:21:50.940 --> 00:21:53.410
This is one of your responsibilities, too.

00:21:54.090 --> 00:21:57.420
Whether or not this sight 
disappears from the academy

00:21:57.820 --> 00:21:59.670
depends on you.

00:23:39.980 --> 00:23:40.770
<b>Next Episode</b>

00:23:40.770 --> 00:24:09.420
<b>Next Episode</b>

00:23:42.160 --> 00:23:45.350
Izumi-senpai, you play <i>PSO2</i>, right?

00:23:45.350 --> 00:23:46.600
Let's play together sometime.

00:23:46.600 --> 00:23:48.720
Tachibana-kun, you're awfully motivated.

00:23:48.720 --> 00:23:52.390
Yeah. A considerate player named 
SORO taught me a bunch of things.

00:23:52.390 --> 00:23:53.820
Oh, really?

00:23:53.820 --> 00:23:56.220
They can be a bit of a pain, though.

00:23:56.220 --> 00:23:57.910
And they can be overbearing 
and sort of scary.

00:23:57.910 --> 00:24:00.680
R-Really? A pain, huh?

00:24:00.680 --> 00:24:03.650
They're probably a busybody 
in real life, too.

00:24:03.650 --> 00:24:05.940
Izumi-senpai? Is something wrong?

00:24:06.290 --> 00:24:07.510
It's nothing!

00:24:07.510 --> 00:24:09.420
Wh-Why are you upset?
